WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.100
Here's the lesson this check hides.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.750
The read is GET directory,
on-premises synchronization.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.490
Microsoft Learn's Graph
reference for that call,

4
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:13.285
Get on-premises directory synchronization,
names its least-privileged permission,

5
00:00:13.285 --> 00:00:17.463
OnPremDirectorySynchronization dot
Read dot All, which looks harmless.

6
00:00:17.463 --> 00:00:21.158
But the same page lists no
application permission for it at all,

7
00:00:21.158 --> 00:00:25.849
and for delegated access says Global
Administrator is the only supported role.

8
00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:30.738
A read-only check, run live, would need
the most powerful role in the tenant.

9
00:00:30.738 --> 00:00:34.626
The kit's design rule is that a
check asks for the least privilege

10
00:00:34.626 --> 00:00:38.513
the question needs, and GET-only
is necessary but not sufficient.

11
00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:40.913
So this check does three
things differently.

12
00:00:40.913 --> 00:00:45.538
It's optional, so it stays out of a
default run and runs only when named.

13
00:00:45.538 --> 00:00:48.963
It prefers an export, saved
by a Global Administrator

14
00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:51.688
who is already signed
in for other reasons.

15
00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:55.685
And it says so: the catalog
names the role and the reason,

16
00:00:55.685 --> 00:00:57.600
before anyone runs it live.
